From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2026 10:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] build/config: do not fail on -Wunused-template

The engine builds with -Werror unconditionally, and clang 23 reports
unused function templates in vendored third-party sources that predate
the diagnostic:

  third_party/dart/third_party/double-conversion/src/bignum.cc:49:12:
    error: unused function template 'BitSize' [-Werror,-Wunused-template]

Only riscv64 hits this in meta-flutter: every other architecture builds
the engine with the clang bundled in the SDK's buildtools, while riscv64
sets CLANG_PATH to the native toolchain, which oe-core has moved to
clang/llvm 23.1.0.

The warning is about third-party code this layer does not maintain, so
disable it rather than carry a patch per vendored source.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific toolchain combination]
Signed-off-by: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
---
diff --git a/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn b/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
--- a/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -738,6 +738,10 @@ if (is_win) {
     # Disables.
     "-Wno-missing-field-initializers",  # "struct foo f = {0};"
     "-Wno-unused-parameter",  # Unused function parameters.
+
+    # clang 23 reports unused function templates in vendored third-party
+    # sources that predate the diagnostic.
+    "-Wno-unused-template",
   ]
 
   if (!is_qnx) {
